---
/**
 * BEYOND ACADEMICS → ACHIEVEMENTS  ·  audit §4.
 *
 * ═══ WHY THIS PAGE EXISTS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * Audit §4, verbatim: "Achievements can then be showcased separately, with major
 * achievements displayed first using high-resolution photographs." The word is
 * SEPARATELY. Achievements previously closed the Sports & Games page, which
 * satisfied "last" but not "separately" — so they moved here, that page now ends
 * on coaching and links across, and the navigation entry that had pointed at a
 * 404 since it was written now resolves.
 *
 * The page runs majors → recognition → full record:
 *
 *   1 Majors       INK   · three award graphics at display size, lead spanning
 *   2 Recognition  ivory · six third-party credentials
 *   3 Record       sand  · sport and academic boards, eleven entries
 *
 * ═══ WHAT THE MOVE MADE ROOM FOR ═══════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * A page of its own holds more than the foot of a sports page could. Two things
 * that were published and appeared NOWHERE on the rebuilt site are now here:
 *
 * · THE THIRD-PARTY RECOGNITION — the Education World district ranking held six
 *   years running, the Microsoft Showcase designation, the Eduserve, Brainfeed
 *   and Kalam awards. docs/01 §34 calls this the school's most under-used asset.
 * · THE ACADEMIC RECORD — the AI Impact Festival win, the Vigyan Manthan and
 *   Science Congress qualifications, the MANAK selections.
 *
 * And two of the three high-resolution award graphics the school has produced —
 * RoboWunder and the National School Innovation ranking — had never been used
 * anywhere either.
 *
 * ⚠ NO BOARD RESULTS, AND THAT IS THE GAP TO CLOSE NEXT. Audit §2E requires
 * them; the school publishes no pass rate, no toppers and no year-on-year data,
 * and `/result/` is only a login portal (docs/01 §119). Nothing on this page
 * estimates them.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import SectionRail from '../../components/academics/SectionRail.astro';

import Majors from '../../components/beyond/achievements/Majors.astro';
import Recognition from '../../components/beyond/achievements/Recognition.astro';
import Boards from '../../components/beyond/achievements/Boards.astro';

/* The awards ceremony in the school hall — the one photograph in the library
   that actually depicts an achievement being received. */
import heroPhoto from '../../assets/photos/sunbeem-4.jpg';
---

<BaseLayout
>
  <PageHero
    src={heroPhoto}
  />

  <SectionRail
    items={[
      { id: 'major', label: 'Major' },
      { id: 'recognition', label: 'Recognition' },
      { id: 'record', label: 'Full record' },
    ]}
  />

  {/* padding-block: 0 — every section carries its own --sb-section-y, and the
      panel adding its own on top is what put a 183px void under the hero on
      three earlier pages. */}
  <div class="u-page-panel ach-panel">
    <Majors />
    <Recognition />
    <Boards />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  div.ach-panel { padding-block: 0; }

  .ach-panel :global(section[id]) {
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--sb-masthead-h) + 24px);
  }
</style>
